📗
  Builds the app, in two steps with the settings between them, as ASP.NET has
  a builder and then an app:

    🌱🐇🏗❗️ ➡️ app      a new app, with the sample's settings declared
    📂 app❗️             the config file and the environment over them
    🍷🐇🏗 app❗️          middleware and routes, from the settings as they now are
📗
🐇 🏗 🍇
  📗 A new app that knows the sample's own settings, and has nothing else yet. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🌱 ➡️ 🍷 🍇
    🆕🍷❗️ ➡️ app

    💭 Bodies here are small JSON documents, so there is no reason to accept a megabyte.
    🎚 app 🔤limits.bodyBytes🔤 16384❗️

    💭 How many todos the list holds.
    🌱 app 🔤todo.capacity🔤 1000 1 1000000❗️
    ↩️ app
  🍉

  📗 Gives *app* the sample's middleware and routes. What they are made from is read from the settings here and now, so it comes after 📂. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🍷 app 🍷 🍇
    💭 Middleware runs in registration order, wrapping everything after it. The logger is
    💭 first, so that it sees every answer, the refusals of the layers behind it included.
    🧱 app 📝 app❗️❗️

    💭 Long answers that are text go out as gzip to a client that takes it. Second, so
    💭 that whatever the layers and routes behind it answer is seen by it.
    🧱 app 🤐 app 🆕🤐❗️❗️❗️

    💭 The headers that make a browser careful with what it is given.
